00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:19.640
or they haven't kind of done like a Colab example.&nbsp;
Like I want people that aren't intimidated by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:25.040
trying that. I don't need them to like be able to&nbsp;
answer every technical question they might have,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:28.600
but what goes a long way with me is like, 'Hey,&nbsp;
I went and like went for it and just tried it.'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:34.760
That's I think something I look for because I&nbsp;
think in these - it moves so quickly that you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:34.760 --> 00:17:38.840
need to know that people are willing to go for it&nbsp;
and try it. Because otherwise, they're going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:38.840 --> 00:17:43.000
fall behind, no matter how technical they are&nbsp;
today. The shelf life of this knowledge is so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:50.040
short that you have to keep trying things and be&nbsp;
brave about entering things that you don't know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:54.080
a lot about. Like when prompt engineering came&nbsp;
along, I didn't know about it, I didn't understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:54.080 --> 00:17:59.480
