00:19:33.320 --> 00:19:37.920
to increase our ability to train models on&nbsp;
the finite amount of compute that we have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:41.400
now? Is that something that you ever&nbsp;
think about? And if not, it's not -"&nbsp;

00:19:41.400 --> 00:19:46.840
"No, no, we think about it a lot. So we don't&nbsp;
- we measure all this. We don't - we can't like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:46.840 --> 00:19:50.840
help you - we can help you use your GPUs better&nbsp;
by measuring if you're using it or not. So we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:50.840 --> 00:19:56.160
actually keep track of like, you know, how much -&nbsp;
if you're fine-tuning - and actually the example&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:56.160 --> 00:20:00.880
you did, if you look at the system metrics, it'll&nbsp;
